-- A WITH may name a section binder the callee READS. Naming one it does not
-- read is the same mistake as naming a parameter it does not take: there is
-- nowhere to put the value, so the override would silently do nothing.
--
-- `unrelated` reads no binder at all; `reads the other one` reads a different
-- binder in the same module.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER
          surcharge  IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
unrelated MEANS 7

GIVETH A NUMBER
`reads the other one` MEANS surcharge PLUS 1

#EVAL unrelated WITH `the rate` IS 5
#EVAL `reads the other one` WITH `the rate` IS 5
